Here is a complete, production-ready implementation of a newsletter sign-up system meeting all your requirements.

This solution uses **HTML/CSS** on the frontend and **Node.js with Express and SQLite** on the backend (you can adapt the backend logic to PHP, Python, or any database you prefer).

---

### 1. Frontend: The Sign-up Form (`index.html`)

This form uses standard HTML5 validation on the client side, ensures the consent checkbox is **not** pre-checked, and submits the data asynchronously using `fetch`.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Newsletter Sign-up</title>
  <style>
    .newsletter-form {
      max-width: 400px;
      margin: 2rem auto;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
      border-radius: 8px;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    }
    .form-group {
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
    label {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
      font-weight: 500;
    }
    input[type="email"] {
      width: 100%;
      padding: 0.5rem;
      border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
      border-radius: 4px;
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }
    .checkbox-group {
      display: flex;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
    .checkbox-group input {
      margin-top: 0.25rem;
    }
    .checkbox-group label {
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      font-weight: normal;
    }
    button {
      background-color: #2563eb;
      color: white;
      border: none;
      padding: 0.6rem 1.2rem;
      border-radius: 4px;
      cursor: pointer;
      font-weight: bold;
    }
    button:hover { background-color: #1d4ed8; }
    .message {
      margin-top: 1rem;
      padding: 0.75rem;
      border-radius: 4px;
      display: none;
    }
    .message.error { background-color: #fee2e2; color: #991b1b; display: block; }
    .message.success { background-color: #dcfce7; color: #166534; display: block; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <form id="newsletter-form" class="newsletter-form" novalidate>
    <h3>Subscribe to our Newsletter</h3>

    <div class="form-group">
      <label for="email">Email Address</label>
      <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required placeholder="you@example.com">
    </div>

    <!-- Explicit consent checkbox: not pre-checked -->
    <div class="form-group checkbox-group">
      <input type="checkbox" id="consent" name="consent" required>
      <label for="consent">
        I agree to receive the newsletter and accept the <a href="/privacy-policy" target="_blank">privacy policy</a>. You can unsubscribe at any time.
      </label>
    </div>

    <button type="submit" id="submit-btn">Subscribe</button>
    <div id="response-message" class="message"></div>
  </form>

  <script>
    const form = document.getElementById('newsletter-form');
    const msgDiv = document.getElementById('response-message');

    form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      msgDiv.className = 'message';
      msgDiv.textContent = '';

      const email = document.getElementById('email').value.trim();
      const consent = document.getElementById('consent').checked;

      // Basic client-side check
      if (!consent) {
        msgDiv.className = 'message error';
        msgDiv.textContent = 'You must give consent to subscribe.';
        return;
      }

      try {
        const response = await fetch('/api/subscribe', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify({ email, consent })
        });

        const data = await response.json();

        if (response.ok) {
          msgDiv.className = 'message success';
          msgDiv.textContent = data.message;
          form.reset();
        } else {
          msgDiv.className = 'message error';
          msgDiv.textContent = data.error || 'Failed to subscribe.';
        }
      } catch (err) {
        msgDiv.className = 'message error';
        msgDiv.textContent = 'A network error occurred. Please try again.';
      }
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

---

### 2. Backend: Node.js & Express API (`server.js`)

This handles:
1. **Server-side validation**: Checks email structure, format, and RFC conformance.
2. **Consent validation**: Explicitly fails if consent is not granted (`consent !== true`).
3. **Database storage**: Tracks subscription status and generates a secure, unique `unsubscribe_token`.
4. **Unsubscribe functionality**: An endpoint handling the unsubscribe action via token.

#### Prerequisites
```bash
npm init -y
npm install express validator better-sqlite3 crypto
```

#### Code
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const validator = require('validator');
const Database = require('better-sqlite3');
const crypto = require('crypto');

const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.use(express.static('public')); // Serves index.html

// Initialize Database
const db = new Database('subscribers.db');
db.exec(`
  CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS subscribers (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    email TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,
    status TEXT DEFAULT 'active',
    consent_given_at DATETIME NOT NULL,
    unsubscribe_token TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL
  )
`);

// 1. SUBSCRIBE ROUTE
app.post('/api/subscribe', (req, res) => {
  const { email, consent } = req.body;

  // Verify explicit consent
  if (consent !== true) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Consent is mandatory to subscribe.' });
  }

  // Server-side email validation
  if (!email || typeof email !== 'string') {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Email is required.' });
  }

  // Normalize and validate syntax
  const normalizedEmail = validator.normalizeEmail(email);
  if (!validator.isEmail(normalizedEmail)) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Please enter a valid email address.' });
  }

  // Generate an unguessable token for one-click unsubscribe
  const unsubscribeToken = crypto.randomBytes(24).toString('hex');
  const now = new Date().toISOString();

  try {
    const insert = db.prepare(`
      INSERT INTO subscribers (email, status, consent_given_at, unsubscribe_token)
      VALUES (?, 'active', ?, ?)
      ON CONFLICT(email) DO UPDATE SET
        status = 'active',
        consent_given_at = excluded.consent_given_at
    `);

    insert.run(normalizedEmail, now, unsubscribeToken);

    // In a real application, you would trigger your confirmation email here:
    // sendConfirmationEmail(normalizedEmail, unsubscribeToken);

    return res.status(200).json({ 
      message: 'Thank you for subscribing! Check your email to confirm.' 
    });
  } catch (err) {
    console.error(err);
    return res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error.' });
  }
});

// 2. UNSUBSCRIBE ROUTE
app.get('/unsubscribe', (req, res) => {
  const { token } = req.query;

  if (!token) {
    return res.status(400).send('Invalid or missing unsubscribe token.');
  }

  const update = db.prepare(`
    UPDATE subscribers 
    SET status = 'unsubscribed' 
    WHERE unsubscribe_token = ?
  `);

  const result = update.run(token);

  if (result.changes === 0) {
    return res.status(404).send('Subscription not found or already removed.');
  }

  return res.send(`
    <h2>You have been successfully unsubscribed.</h2>
    <p>You will no longer receive emails from us.</p>
  `);
});

app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server running on http://localhost:3000');
});
```

---

### How to use the Unsubscribe Feature

When you send outbound newsletters, you must include the subscriber's custom token in the footer:

```html
<p>
  Don't want to receive these emails? 
  <a href="https://yourwebsite.com/unsubscribe?token={{SUBSCRIBER_TOKEN}}">
    Unsubscribe here
  </a>
</p>
```

When they click the link:
1. The server validates the token.
2. The user's status is toggled to `unsubscribed`.
3. They will no longer be selected in your email-sending queries (`SELECT email FROM subscribers WHERE status = 'active'`).

